How to make Manjaro auto-suspend even when logged out:

You can enable system-wide suspend by setting up logind.conf (used by systemd-logind).

1. Edit the systemd logind config:

	sudo nano /etc/systemd/logind.conf

Look for these lines and uncomment + set values (or add them if not there):

	IdleAction=suspend
	IdleActionSec=15min

This means: after 15 minutes of system idle time (regardless of login state), the system will suspend.

2. Restart systemd-logind:

	sudo systemctl restart systemd-logind